From 4ea7552160a40bc8b8128c5d6e819bb49496af6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 05:49:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Close every NotImplementedException site and Application's
 lifecycle tail

Class B is now empty: no NotImplementedException throw site remains in either
shipped project.

PropertyGrid/GridEntry (11 of the 15 sites). GridEntry declares
ITypeDescriptorContext - what a type converter or UI type editor is handed while
a property is edited - but every member of that contract threw, so any conversion
that consulted its context failed at runtime. Container now comes from the edited
component's site (walking up parents, then the owning grid's site), Instance is
the value owner, GetService answers for itself and defers to the sites, and
OnComponentChanging/OnComponentChanged drive IComponentChangeService, returning
false on a cancelled checkout. PropertyDescriptor was an override that could only
ever be null; it now resolves through TypeDescriptor, which is what the change
notifications report. SetValue brackets the write with those notifications, so a
refused change leaves the property untouched. The six IComPropertyBrowser members
commit the open GTK cell editor, close it, focus the grid, and load/save the view
state - the state pair takes WinForms' null-key path always, because the shim's
RegistryKey holds no values off Windows.

Four isolated sites: ArrangedElement.Handle is IntPtr.Zero (a layout participant
is not a window), DataGridViewCellCollection's IList indexer routes to the typed
one, DataGridViewCellStyle's ICloneable.Clone routes to Clone, and
DataGridViewCellLinkedList - a stub with no storage, whose GetEnumerator threw -
is a working head-insertion list.

Three Class C defects found while testing the above are fixed with them:
InPropertySet returned a constant true; assigning SelectedObject (not
SelectedObjects) never populated the grid nor raised SelectedObjectsChanged; and
a *missing* BrowsableAttribute was read as "not browsable", so an object carrying
no design-time attributes displayed no properties at all.

Graphics.SetClip(Region) through the region's path. A region built from a
GraphicsPath kept only the path's bounding rectangle in its band list, so
clipping to an ellipse clipped to its box. The region now tracks whether the path
is still its exact description, and ApplyClip replays that path into Cairo -
the replay loop pulled out of DrawPathCore, with text contributing glyph outlines
rather than painted glyphs when the target is a clip. Combining still falls back
to bands; that limit is recorded.

Application gains Idle, Restart, ProductName/ProductVersion/CompanyName,
RenderWithVisualStyles and VisualStyleState. GTK has no queue-drained
notification, so Idle is sampled by a 50 ms GLib source installed only while
something is subscribed: raised once per lull, re-armed when events reappear.

Covered by PropertyGridBrowserFunctionalTests, ApplicationResidualSurfaceFunctional-
Tests, DataGridViewCollectionMembersFunctionalTests and
GraphicsRegionPathClipFunctionalTests (the corner pixel of an inscribed ellipse is
the oracle - no reported state distinguishes the two clip behaviours). Two tests
that pinned the old throwing behaviour were rewritten to pin the new one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
